<task id="034" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Inbound communication and document ingestion create through the system principal (FR-21 part b)</title>
    <phase>3 W3 Product creators onto the service</phase>
    <gate>019 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api; tags include bff-api, communication, documents, ownership; inbound paths carry race-proof dedupe and documented ownership exceptions (data-mutation, security-adjacent); adds tests at KEEP paths (TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Four ingestion creators with race-proof dedupe, unfiled-communication ownership exceptions and thread filing; judgment needed about what the service must support versus what stays in the ingestor.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W3-server</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>019</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, communication, documents, ownership, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>10-14 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Route inbound communication and document ingestion through `RecordCreationService` with the SYSTEM principal: `MessagingIngestor` (`Services/Communication/Channels/MessagingIngestor.cs`, create ~:265), `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` (`Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs`, communication via `CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync` ~:874, attachment documents ~:1135/~:1170, archived .eml document ~:1365), `EmailAttachmentProcessor` (`Services/Email/EmailAttachmentProcessor.cs`, `_documentService.CreateDocumentAsync` ~:311) and `EmailUploadCaptureService` (`Services/Communication/EmailUploadCaptureService.cs`, `CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync` ~:194). Unfiled communications keep the creator (registry exception); direct threads stay an exception; a census test lists each of the four as routed.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, inbound email/messaging ingestion and Dataverse ownership. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Inbound communications and the documents created from them are created by the service with the system principal and the standard invariants; the UNIQUE-key race-proof dedupe and the unfiled-communication creator-owner exception are preserved; the census lists each ingestor as routed.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-21 (part b), FR-07, FR-11. Today: `MessagingIngestor` builds a `sprk_communication` with NO owner ("unfiled communications keep their creator as owner", owner round 10 item 8, 2026-10-03; Census: a Permanent waiver in `RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests`) and calls `_genericEntityService.CreateAsync` (~:265); `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` and `EmailUploadCaptureService` create communications through `ICommunicationDataverseService.CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync`, whose UNIQUE key on the internet message id makes concurrent deliveries idempotent; attachment documents and the archived .eml document are created with `ApplyOwner(doc, owner)` ("owned like its communication") through `_genericEntityService.CreateAsync`; `EmailAttachmentProcessor` creates documents through `_documentService.CreateDocumentAsync`. Filing happens later via `IncomingAssociationResolver` (`UnfiledOwnership.KeepCreator`, ~:247 and ~:517) and `ReparentAsync`. UAC-r2 PR #2110 also edits `CommunicationService.cs`; do not edit that file in this task.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/MessagingIngestor.cs (create ~:265)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs (communication create ~:874; documents ~:1135, ~:1170, ~:1365; ApplyOwner)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Email/EmailAttachmentProcessor.cs (document create ~:311)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/EmailUploadCaptureService.cs (communication create ~:194)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRules.cs (sprk_communication: KeepCreator-when-unfiled exception; direct-thread exception; sprk_document owned-like-communication rule; each with rationale)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs (list the four as routed; replace the Permanent waiver with the named registry exception; run /conflict-check, UAC-r2 also edits this file)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingAssociationResolver.cs (KeepCreator ~:247, ~:517)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.cs (system principal, tasks 013-016)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/Communication/EmailUploadCaptureSeamTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/Communication/MessagingSpineSeamTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/Communication/GoldenMisfileRegressionTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/IngestionThroughServiceTests.cs (each ingestor creates through the service; unfiled keeps creator; filed document owned like its communication; dedupe holds)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="019" status="required">W2 service deployed and reviewed.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 (path A, spec ADR Tensions)">Scope: authorization. Ingestors are non-HTTP system callers; the system principal skips only the as-caller checks. Inbound filing authorization (who may file a message under a record) stays in the association resolver and the existing communication routes; the ingestors gain no new inline checks and lose none.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: failures. Ingestors keep their existing failure handling (message-level retry/dead-letter, per-attachment failure logging); a service refusal maps to the same handling as today's create failure; no raw upstream text is stored in a communication row's status fields.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: identity. System principal, app-only under the managed identity; `RequestedBy` is recorded only when a user is known (an upload by a user for `EmailUploadCaptureService`). Inbound external senders are never a principal. Unfiled communications keep the CREATOR (the app identity) per the accepted exception; do not assign a user.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. Ingestors obtain the already-registered scoped service within their existing per-message scope; no new registration; no static service locator.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">Scope: job idempotency. The UNIQUE-key race-proof create (`CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync`) is the dedupe contract: a concurrent duplicate delivery must still resolve to the existing communication id. The service must either support that contract (a documented create option) or the ingestor keeps calling the race-proof method for the communication row only (see escalation). Never retry blindly after an ambiguous failure (NFR-03).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 (spec)">Scope: ingestion creates. Fail closed: an unresolved owner for a FILED row refuses and writes nothing; an UNFILED communication takes the registry exception (creator), never a guessed owner. A message with no resolvable parent is never silently filed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08 / CLAUDE.md §8.5">Scope: coordination. UAC-r2 PR #2110 edits CommunicationService.cs and the census tests; run /conflict-check FIRST. This task must not edit CommunicationService.cs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: BFF publish. Placement Justification in the PR; fresh-master publish-size delta per §10.4; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`; no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added or modified. KEEP paths; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;; no DI-registration tests. Existing seam tests change only to follow a moved dependency, never by weakening an assertion. Cover the stated contract plus the named edge cases only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

