  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; read spec FR-21 and the four ingestors; re-grep every `_genericEntityService.CreateAsync`, `CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync` and `CreateDocumentAsync` call in Services/Communication/ and Services/Email/.</step>
    <step order="1">Run /conflict-check (UAC-r2 PR #2110: CommunicationService.cs and census tests). Record the result. Escalate if a PR changes these ingestors' create sites.</step>
    <step order="2">Inventory, in the task notes, each ingestor's create sites and their current owner behaviour (KeepCreator when unfiled, ApplyOwner for documents, direct threads) and the registry rule that will carry each, with rationale.</step>
    <step order="3">Write failing tests first: each ingestor creates through the service with the system principal; an unfiled communication keeps the creator (no ownerid set); a communication filed under a Matter gets the record-first team and the I-1 stamp; a document created from a communication is owned like its communication; a concurrent duplicate delivery returns the existing communication id with one row; census lists the four as routed.</step>
    <step order="4">Convert the document creates first (attachment documents, archived .eml, EmailAttachmentProcessor), then the communication creates. Keep `ApplyOwner` semantics ("owned like its communication") as an explicit service input (carried owner), not a re-resolution, so attachment children match their parent.</step>
    <step order="5">Resolve the race-proof dedupe per the ADR-036 constraint; document the chosen option and its evidence in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="6">Update RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests: the four listed as routed; the Permanent waiver for unfiled communications becomes the named registry exception.</step>
    <step order="7">Build; run Communication seam tests (EmailUploadCapture, MessagingSpine, GoldenMisfire, ThreadResolver), the SecureChildOwnership communication tests, SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests; publish-size delta; CVE check.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the unified service cannot honour the UNIQUE-key race-proof create (concurrent duplicate deliveries must resolve to one row) without a new create option, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with the two options (add a documented create option vs keep the race-proof call for the communication row only and route everything else).</trigger>
    <trigger>If /conflict-check shows UAC-r2 PR #2110 edits the same lines of these ingestors or the census tests, STOP and ask the human to sequence the work.</trigger>
    <trigger>If an ingestor creates a table that has no RecordTableRules entry and no obvious exception, STOP and escalate; do not add an exception without a stated rationale.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Grep `_genericEntityService.CreateAsync` (MessagingIngestor.cs ~:265; IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs ~:1135, ~:1170, ~:1365), `CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync` (IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs ~:874; EmailUploadCaptureService.cs ~:194) and `_documentService.CreateDocumentAsync` (EmailAttachmentProcessor.cs ~:311). Existing tests: tests/integration/seam/Communication/ (EmailUploadCaptureSeamTests, MessagingSpineSeamTests) and tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs (Permanent waiver for unfiled communications).</existing>
    <extension>Yes for production code: the ingestors call the existing service; exceptions are registry rows; no new production file. The only new file is a test class, because the existing communication seam suites must pass unchanged and none asserts that ingestion goes through the service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Inbound communications and the documents created from them stay outside the service, so their filed rows skip mapping, the standard stamp and the search-index default, and the census keeps a Permanent waiver instead of a named, rationalised exception (spec FR-21 acceptance).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
