  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`MessagingIngestor`, `IncomingCommunicationProcessor`, `EmailAttachmentProcessor` and `EmailUploadCaptureService` create their communication and document rows through `RecordCreationService` with the system principal (or, for the communication row only, through the documented race-proof option recorded in the task notes), and the census test lists each as routed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An unfiled inbound communication keeps the creator as owner via a NAMED registry exception with a written rationale; the direct-thread exception is a named registry rule; the Permanent waiver in the census test is replaced by them.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A communication filed under a Matter is owned by the record-first team and carries the I-1 stamp; a document created from a communication is owned like its communication (carried owner), asserted by a test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Concurrent duplicate deliveries of the same internet message id still resolve to exactly one communication row (existing dedupe contract preserved), asserted by a test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a filed row whose owner cannot be resolved is refused and writes nothing; an unfiled communication never receives a guessed user or team owner.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no inbound external sender or message field can select the system principal or set `RequestedBy` (asserted by a test or a recorded grep).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build 0 errors; Communication seam tests, SecureChildOwnership communication tests, SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests* and RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests pass; publish-size delta, CVE result and /conflict-check result recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-21 part b, FR-07, FR-11, NFR-08. System creators for To Do, task, Signal and Decision Record are task 033. The notification outbox exception is assessed in task 060.</notes>

